From: Gleb Pesin <dormancygrace@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] sophgo: hand PWR_SEQ1 to its GPIO

With the pinmux on PWR_GPIO[3], the PWR_SEQ1 pad still followed the RTC
power sequencer: driving the GPIO low left the pad high, so the NanoKVM
PCIe HDD LED input never changed. Writing 0x11 to RTCSYS_IO 0x78, as
Sipeed's cvi_board_init() does, gives the pad to the GPIO.

---
--- a/board/sophgo/licheerv_nano/board.c
+++ b/board/sophgo/licheerv_nano/board.c
@@ -27,5 +27,12 @@
 	writel(0x5649, phy + 0x0c);
 	writel(0x0000, wrap + 4); /* Return control to the MAC MDIO bus. */
 
+	/* PWR_SEQ1 stays with the RTC power sequencer, whatever its pinmux,
+	 * until this RTCSYS_IO register hands it to PWR_GPIO[3] (Sipeed's
+	 * board init writes the same value). NanoKVM PCIe reads the host
+	 * HDD LED on that GPIO; Linux sets the pinmux.
+	 */
+	writel(0x11, (void __iomem *)0x05027078);
+
 	return 0;
 }
